WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:04.870
Floods can carry dysentery and typhoid into drinking water and food.

2
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.989
Both come from germs in human faeces, and both can be serious,

3
00:00:08.989 --> 00:00:10.829
especially for young children.

4
00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:13.819
But they can be prevented, and they can be treated.

5
00:00:13.989 --> 00:00:15.940
Here is how to protect your family.

6
00:00:16.834 --> 00:00:21.864
The germs live in the faeces of sick people, and of some people who look well.

7
00:00:21.994 --> 00:00:26.594
When floodwater or overflowing latrines reach wells, tanks and food,

8
00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:27.824
the germs get in.

9
00:00:28.034 --> 00:00:31.344
Dirty hands and flies carry them onto food too.

10
00:00:32.254 --> 00:00:37.044
Dysentery is diarrhoea with blood in it, often with fever and stomach cramps.

11
00:00:37.294 --> 00:00:42.534
Typhoid starts slowly: a fever that rises over several days and does not go away,

12
00:00:42.534 --> 00:00:45.444
with headache, stomach pain and weakness.

13
00:00:45.614 --> 00:00:48.364
Without treatment, typhoid can kill.

14
00:00:49.258 --> 00:00:51.938
First, make drinking water safe.

15
00:00:51.938 --> 00:00:55.328
Bring the water to a rolling boil, with big bubbles,

16
00:00:55.338 --> 00:00:59.737
then let it cool with the lid on, and keep it in a clean, covered container.

17
00:00:59.737 --> 00:01:04.608
If you cannot boil it, use water treatment tablets exactly as the packet says.

18
00:01:05.518 --> 00:01:09.268
Second, wash your hands with soap and clean water.

19
00:01:09.397 --> 00:01:11.788
Wet your hands and rub in soap.

20
00:01:11.878 --> 00:01:17.508
Scrub every part: palms, backs, between the fingers and under the nails.

21
00:01:17.597 --> 00:01:19.868
Rinse, and let them dry in the air.

22
00:01:20.038 --> 00:01:23.838
Do it after the toilet, after cleaning a child, before cooking,

23
00:01:23.838 --> 00:01:26.348
and before eating or feeding a child.

24
00:01:27.226 --> 00:01:29.146
Third, make food safe.

25
00:01:29.146 --> 00:01:31.856
Cook food well and eat it while it is hot.

26
00:01:31.986 --> 00:01:34.546
Wash fruit with safe water and peel it.

27
00:01:34.546 --> 00:01:37.176
Keep food covered, away from flies.

28
00:01:37.385 --> 00:01:41.015
Anyone sick with diarrhoea or fever should not cook for others.

29
00:01:41.878 --> 00:01:44.508
Fourth, keep faeces away from water.

30
00:01:44.797 --> 00:01:49.868
Always use a latrine, never open ground, and keep latrines far from wells.

31
00:01:49.957 --> 00:01:54.267
Put children's faeces in the latrine too, and wash your hands afterwards.

32
00:01:55.138 --> 00:01:56.978
If someone has diarrhoea with blood,

33
00:01:56.978 --> 00:02:00.928
start ORS straight away and go to a health facility.

34
00:02:00.938 --> 00:02:05.568
Anyone with a fever that lasts more than three days should see a health worker too.

35
00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:10.568
Dysentery and typhoid need the right medicine from a health worker: take all of it,

36
00:02:10.568 --> 00:02:11.928
even when you feel better,

37
00:02:11.928 --> 00:02:15.637
and never buy antibiotics without a health worker's advice.

38
00:02:15.647 --> 00:02:19.848
Go at once if the person is very weak or sleepy, cannot drink,

39
00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:21.718
or has severe stomach pain.

40
00:02:22.606 --> 00:02:25.925
Where health workers offer the typhoid vaccine, take it,

41
00:02:25.925 --> 00:02:28.556
and keep boiling water and washing hands.

42
00:02:28.606 --> 00:02:31.566
Safe water, clean hands, safe food.

43
00:02:31.566 --> 00:02:33.036
Share this with your family.
